,32}$ is a subset of $A.$\n\nIn the rest of the options, the set $B$ has elements that are not in $A,$ meaning that it is not a subset of $A.$" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300945 13194139534644 true] [17592186300944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300946 13194139534644 true] [17592186300944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300947 13194139534644 true] [17592186300944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300948 13194139534644 true] [17592186300944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300949 13194139534644 true] [17592186300944 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534644 true] [17592186300944 1041 "selection" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300944 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300948 13194139534644 true] [17592186300944 1110 #uuid "1864bcf5-a777-5135-8aef-787b82f38f91" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300945 1034 "B={0,1,2,4,6,8}" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300945 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534644 true] [17592186300945 1111 #uuid "5892d4db-ee17-5a9b-bb7d-4dabe3624e20" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300946 1034 "B={-1,0,1,2,4,6}" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300946 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534644 true] [17592186300946 1111 #uuid "87bb18dc-9899-5965-962b-0ce6916f989c" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300947 1034 "B={1,3,5,7,9}" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300947 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534644 true] [17592186300947 1111 #uuid "38af7345-898b-5fad-87ca-5b2b33366056" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300948 1034 "B={2,6,12,14,32}" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300948 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534644 true] [17592186300948 1111 #uuid "18a1bd9e-7f78-57c3-b75d-8ce5a365964f" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300949 1034 "B={2,4,6,7}" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300949 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534644 true] [17592186300949 1111 #uuid "17e08c17-c0a4-5c01-92e5-c8cea1cf8431" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300950 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300951 13194139534644 true] [17592186300950 1089 "q-37267" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300950 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534644 true] [17592186300950 1100 "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,…}$ and $B={5n∣n\\in N,3\\le n\\le 7}?$\n\n- $B⊆A$\n- $A⊆B$\n- $A⊈B$\n- $A⊇B$" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300950 1113 #uuid "5f2ce395-36f1-5103-8a97-86f354e329cb" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300950 1145 "First, we must find the elements of the set $B.$ Substituting the values $n\\in {3,4,5,6,7}$ into the formula $5n,$ we get the following elements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=3 & \\,⇒\\,5(3)=15 \\\\ n=4 & \\,⇒\\,5(4)=20 \\\\ n=5 & \\,⇒\\,5(5)=25 \\\\ n=6 & \\,⇒\\,5(6)=30 \\\\ n=7 & \\,⇒\\,5(7)=35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nB={15,20,25,30,35}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false, while $A⊈B$ is true. For example, $5\\in A$ but $5\\notin B.$\n\n- $A⊇B$ is equivalent to $B⊆A,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, III, and IV only\"." 13194139534644 true] [17592186300951 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300952 13194139534644 true] [17592186300951 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300953 13194139534644 true] [17592186300951 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300954 13194139534644 true] [17592186300951 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300955 13194139534644 true] [17592186300951 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300956 13194139534644 true] [17592186300951 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534644 true] [17592186300951 1041 "selection" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300951 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300953 13194139534644 true] [17592186300951 1110 #uuid "a2cd607a-2d8a-59d9-925b-b70565bf262c" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300952 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300952 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300952 1111 #uuid "6bd53d33-1c8e-534e-9ce6-4529042d038f" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300953 1034 "I, III, and IV only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300953 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300953 1111 #uuid "913cbce1-d5c3-528b-a007-ec79a69a2193" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300954 1034 "III and IV only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300954 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300954 1111 #uuid "63d1dcb1-9405-5992-ac49-781495952da9" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300955 1034 "I, II, and IV only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300955 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300955 1111 #uuid "28c111ac-4ff1-53f3-b75f-8dbc64b928af" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300956 1034 "I, II, and III only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300956 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300956 1111 #uuid "cefdc396-cdb8-534a-94b9-3b014581773a" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300957 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300958 13194139534644 true] [17592186300957 1089 "q-506" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300957 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534644 true] [17592186300957 1100 "Which of the following are subsets of $R?$\n\n- ${Q}^{+}$ (the set of positive rationals)\n- ${Z}^{-}$ (the set of negative integers)\n- $N$" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300957 1113 #uuid "1c9ea526-3175-579e-bce7-db2dce376c08" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300957 1145 "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Q}^{+}$ is  a subset of $R.$ Every positive rational number is a real number.\n\n- ${Z}^{-}$ is a subset of $R.$ Every negative integer number is a real number.\n\n- $N$ a subset of $R.$ Every natural number is a real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." 13194139534644 true] [17592186300958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300959 13194139534644 true] [17592186300958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300960 13194139534644 true] [17592186300958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300961 13194139534644 true] [17592186300958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300962 13194139534644 true] [17592186300958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300963 13194139534644 true] [17592186300958 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534644 true] [17592186300958 1041 "selection" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300958 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300959 13194139534644 true] [17592186300958 1110 #uuid "2783eb9e-a3b8-546f-9d63-ec7ede85ec61" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300959 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300959 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300959 1111 #uuid "9d6c89f0-2a1a-5531-b5d8-831e882897bd" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300960 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300960 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300960 1111 #uuid "e6865ba6-79cb-5696-ab09-d0be9337b7cf" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300961 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300961 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300961 1111 #uuid "639e0609-5927-50e2-922f-0b5aa58cc005" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300962 1034 "I only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300962 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300962 1111 #uuid "888a6d2c-da5e-5d94-b324-cd6d72385bc9" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300963 1034 "III only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300963 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300963 1111 #uuid "a1d2d22b-0b13-5678-876c-b0cb42f1ec3f" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300964 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300965 13194139534644 true] [17592186300964 1089 "q-80806" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300964 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534644 true] [17592186300964 1100 "Find all of the subsets of $T={-1,0,1}.$" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300964 1113 #uuid "17fc06b1-e354-5e82-b08b-7057469ae185" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300964 1145 "To find every subset of $T,$ we list out every combination of elements within $T.$ \n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/assets/03bdaa1b1033d662675e8b594fbc6ed2376b43dd71e28af7a8bf61d1ff17a012.png)\n\nNote that we must include the