e] [17592186300986 1041 "selection" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300986 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300991 13194139534644 true] [17592186300986 1110 #uuid "bda17121-15f8-5fcc-ae39-e0cf752e6d29" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300987 1034 "Q⊆R" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300987 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534644 true] [17592186300987 1111 #uuid "0c5213fe-c035-5fec-a59a-ef4f9270f5e8" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300988 1034 "N⊆Q" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300988 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534644 true] [17592186300988 1111 #uuid "85e6b4d8-a6ea-566f-9562-99e396f1006c" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300989 1034 "Z⊆R" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300989 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534644 true] [17592186300989 1111 #uuid "1e79add0-ea94-5476-a9be-ae0681788037" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300990 1034 "N⊆C" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300990 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534644 true] [17592186300990 1111 #uuid "47cdfd95-3adc-55de-8dc8-6ffad711e645" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300991 1034 "Z⊆N" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300991 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534644 true] [17592186300991 1111 #uuid "ac99c84f-92d3-5525-a082-91a3afffe877" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300992 1017 #edb/ref 17592186300993 13194139534644 true] [17592186300992 1089 "q-80812" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300992 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534644 true] [17592186300992 1100 "Which of the following are subsets of ${Q}^{+}$  (the set of positive rational numbers)?\n\n- ${Q}_{0}^{+}$ (the set of non-negative rational numbers)\n- $N$\n- $Z$" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300992 1113 #uuid "bc2578ed-7aae-5f12-a163-5aa37a8919bf" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300992 1145 "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Q}_{0}^{+}$ is not a subset of ${Q}^{+}.$ For example, $0\\in {Q}_{0}^{+}$ but $0\\notin {Q}^{+}.$\n\n- $N$ is a subset of ${Q}^{+}.$ Indeed, every natural number is also a positive rational number.\n\n- $Z$ is not a subset of ${Q}^{+}.$ For example, $-1\\in Z$ but $-1\\notin {Q}^{+}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139534644 true] [17592186300993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300994 13194139534644 true] [17592186300993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300995 13194139534644 true] [17592186300993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300996 13194139534644 true] [17592186300993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300997 13194139534644 true] [17592186300993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186300998 13194139534644 true] [17592186300993 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534644 true] [17592186300993 1041 "selection" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300993 1104 #edb/ref 17592186300998 13194139534644 true] [17592186300993 1110 #uuid "6d28e25c-b5bf-5439-a808-108dc7be28d0" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300994 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300994 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300994 1111 #uuid "a5204b6b-e656-508f-b2f4-53c124882bb6" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300995 1034 "I only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300995 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300995 1111 #uuid "97ee8bc7-80dc-5894-837c-6111723e5693" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300996 1034 "III only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300996 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300996 1111 #uuid "09668d25-9b8f-5542-abcf-265eeba168aa" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300997 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300997 1111 #uuid "051356c2-a92a-55b2-aef2-e1792c93ce19" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300998 1034 "II only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300998 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186300998 1111 #uuid "e939d068-7d4e-56c3-837c-777d90860410" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300999 1017 #edb/ref 17592186301000 13194139534644 true] [17592186300999 1089 "q-80845" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300999 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534644 true] [17592186300999 1100 "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={n\\in Z∣n+1\\ge -1}$ and $B={n\\in Z∣n-2\\ge -4}?$\n\n- $A⊆B$\n- $B⊆A$\n- $B⊈A$\n- $B⊇A$" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300999 1113 #uuid "9a90c52c-818b-5155-a8eb-42e1d51e8eb9" 13194139534644 true] [17592186300999 1145 "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all the integer numbers that satisfy the inequality $n+1\\ge -1,$ that is to say, $n\\ge -2.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nA={-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5,6,…}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality $n-2\\ge -4,$ That is to say, $n\\ge -2.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nB={-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5,6,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is true. Every element in the set $A$ is an element of the set $B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true, while $B⊈A$ is false. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\n- $B⊇A$ is equivalent to $A⊆B,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and IV only\"." 13194139534644 true] [17592186301000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301001 13194139534644 true] [17592186301000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301002 13194139534644 true] [17592186301000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301003 13194139534644 true] [17592186301000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301004 13194139534644 true] [17592186301000 1000 #edb/ref 17592186301005 13194139534644 true] [17592186301000 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534644 true] [17592186301000 1041 "selection" 13194139534644 true] [17592186301000 1104 #edb/ref 17592186301005 13194139534644 true] [17592186301000 1110 #uuid "aa18f640-0d06-58ad-a0c0-856ff8c6e42a" 13194139534644 true] [17592186301001 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534644 true] [17592186301001 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534644 true] [17592186301001 1111 #uuid "07cefd1a-a90f-5344-b0af-d3883e1ae213" 13194139534644 true] [17592186301002 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534644 true] [17592